'' --no-module-cache NEITHER READS NOR WRITES (RFC-0005 §4): -v reports no module and the
'' program still builds; and a cached build straight after misses both modules as new, so
'' the first stored nothing -- asked of the cache's behaviour, since an entry's file names
'' carry hashes no test can spell.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-off/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-off
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/modcache => build/.mct-off
'' STEP: --no-module-cache -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-off/libs build/.mct-off/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-off/app.exe
'' STEP-NOT: module acme
'' ARGS: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-off/libs build/.mct-off/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-off/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.leaf: miss (new)
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.middle: miss (new)
'' RUN: build/.mct-off/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  14
